	"_comment": "Where each body carries the weapons that were modelled for the Atlas MX (#108): the roof turret, the front tools (ram, spear/forklift, grinder) and the auxiliary gun. Authoritative combat geometry and the drawn models read the same record through WeaponMounts, so changing any value is a gameplay change (bump WireCodec.BUILD). Bodies: sawblade (any wheeled or tracked body drawn as the Sawblade tank), scorpion (the hex walker) and box (the plain placeholder hull). Atlas MX and Bracken are the authored originals and use no mount. Offsets are hull source metres (X right, Y up, -Z forward, origin at the hull centre; multiply by the bot scale for game metres). A mount places the Atlas-frame weapon at offset + scale x its Atlas position. riser is the height, in turret metres before the scale, of the drawn pedestal that carries the turret ring over deck fittings; coupler is the length, in tool metres before the scale, of the drawn rails that join the tool's back plate to the body (both presentation only).",
